(CHAPTER 1 | MODULE 8.0: MANDALA THEORY OF FOREIGN POLICY AND THE SIXFOLD ROYAL) Tj
T*
(STRATEGY \(SHADGUNYA\)) Tj
T*
(========================================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(BOOK VI, CHAPTER 1: THE SAPTANGA THEORY OF THE SEVEN LIMBS OF STATE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(According to the Saptanga theory expounded in this compendium, a sovereign state) Tj
T*
(is constituted by seven interdependent organic limbs \(Prakritis\):) Tj
T*
(1. Swamin \(The Sovereign Ruler or King\)) Tj
T*
(2. Amatya \(The Council of Ministers and High Officials\)) Tj
T*
(3. Janapada \(The Territory and its Settled Population\)) Tj
T*
(4. Durga \(The Fortified Capital and Defensive Strongholds\)) Tj
T*
(5. Kosha \(The Royal Treasury and Financial Reserves\)) Tj
T*
(6. Danda or Bala \(The Standing Army and Coercive Authority\)) Tj
T*
(7. Mitra \(The Steadfast Foreign Ally\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Operational Compliance Note \(Ref-5-08\): All personnel and automated auditing) Tj
T*
(systems reviewing 'Compendium of Classical Statecraft & Philosophy: Arthashastra &) Tj
T*
(Gita Selections' must verify the numerical thresholds and procedural steps stated) Tj
T*
(on Page 8 above. Any deviation from the explicit parameters documented in this) Tj
T*
(section requires formal written escalation.) Tj
T*
ET
