(BOOK I, CHAPTER 16: CLASSIFICATION AND AUTHORITY OF ENVOYS \(DUTAS\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In diplomatic missions, envoys \(Dutas\) are classified into exactly three distinct) Tj
T*
(categories based on their level of authority:) Tj
T*
(1. Nisrishtarthah: A Plenipotentiary Ambassador endowed with full ministerial) Tj
T*
(qualifications and discretionary authority to negotiate treaties.) Tj
T*
(2. Parimitarthah: An Envoy Extraordinary entrusted with a strictly limited,) Tj
T*
(predefined mission.) Tj
T*
(3. Shasanaharah: A Royal Messenger or Bearer of Dispatches authorized only to) Tj
T*
(deliver written decrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Operational Compliance Note \(Ref-5-19\): All personnel and automated auditing) Tj
T*
(systems reviewing 'Compendium of Classical Statecraft & Philosophy: Arthashastra &) Tj
T*
(Gita Selections' must verify the numerical thresholds and procedural steps stated) Tj
T*
